ladspa: stop and join the worker thread when the plugin is dropped

Every instance spawned a worker thread whose loop never exited and polled the
input queue every few milliseconds. LADSPA cleanup() drops the plugin, but the
thread kept running, so each instantiate/cleanup cycle (e.g. a PipeWire
filter-chain waking up from suspend) leaked one busy-polling thread.

Add a stop flag checked by the worker loop and a Drop impl that sets it and
joins the thread. Audio processing is unchanged. The new unit test instantiates
and drops several mono and stereo instances and checks /proc/self/task.

